{"kind":"assert","text":"OPS-1 rulings on request 9dd99701. Start the source edits.\n\n1. Offers. Smoke takes its expectation from the tracked config of each\nWorker. A config that declares DEMO_START_CONFIG must answer the offer\nwith 200 and the exact configured register reference. A config without\nit must answer 404. Add no expected-offer input. A kept live offer that\nthe tracked config omits then fails smoke, and that failure is correct:\nit is an untracked setting. wrangler.commons.jsonc also declares the\noffer, so the rule covers it if the command accepts that config.\n\n2. Legacy mode. Add no mode input and no refusal. The command deploys\nthe tracked value. I read the live artroom-scope version 29fffb5f at\n16:05 EST today: SCOPE_INDEX_MODE is register. The tracked file says\nregister. Every deployment since 9 November used the tracked file with\n--keep-vars, so no enforce value is live to overwrite. A move of legacy\nto enforce is a reviewed edit of the tracked file, never a flag. The\ncomment at wrangler.artroom-scope.jsonc lines 11 and 12 is stale. Leave\nthe file alone in OPS-1. The identifiers cutover retires this Worker's\nrooms, and I track the comment there.\nGeneral rule for the runbook section: the tracked config states every\nnonsecret variable that the command sets. --keep-vars preserves only a\nvariable that the tracked config omits. An expected register stays\nread-only smoke context.\n\n3. Partial result. Approved as you propose. A reported version with a\nfailed hash, output or receipt check gives a distinct nonzero exit and a\npartial record with the version, head, config and available hashes,\nwritten outside the checkout. The batch stops. The command never retries\nand never rolls back. A smoke failure keeps the deployment receipt and\nreports the failure. The first operator action on a partial record is\nto reconcile that version before another run. State that in the runbook.\nYou choose the hash method. It must compare stable module names and\nexact code, text, wasm and data bytes, exclude the generated README and\nthe maps, and name whether it proves the dry-run output or the upload.\n\nPaths. Nine paths with the evidence manifest are in scope. Main is now\n810905c9 (documentation group D). It changes docs/operate-a-service.md\nby one link. Merge main before you edit the page, and add the section\nbefore \"## Roll back\". Planner group F will add one paragraph after\n\"Deploy new source\" in the same page. The later head merges the earlier\none. OPS-1 and OPS-2 each add their own line to scripts/test.mjs.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}